# Definition of Done

A page is not done because it visually resembles a mockup.

It is done only when:
- desktop + tablet + mobile are implemented
- approved real copy is used where available
- missing facts are visibly flagged
- keyboard navigation works
- focus states are visible
- contrast is acceptable
- responsive images are optimized
- metadata is complete
- analytics events are wired where specified
- form success/error states work
- no console errors
- no known hydration errors
- key browser widths tested
- page passes product-owner review

Performance target:
- LCP <= 2.5s
- INP <= 200ms
- CLS <= 0.1
- production Lighthouse performance target >= 90 on representative pages

Accessibility target:
- WCAG 2.2 AA

Critical E2E journeys:
1. Home → Software → Work → Start Project → Submit → confirmation
2. Home → Academy → Program → Apply → Submit → confirmation
3. Insight → relevant Solution → Start Project
